{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-94807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $K$ be the set of all $2\\times 1$ matrices $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],$ such that $x,y\\in R$ and $x+y=1.$  Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because **the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K.$** *  \n\nIndeed, adding the entries of the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix yields $0+0=0\\ne 1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- addition of matrices is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- addition and scalar multiplication of matrices  satisfy the distributive laws. $✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices  is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot A=A$ for all $A\\in K.$ $\\,✓$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4648cd819d2f86e7a3e563df5e7fd1d268be7bb1f3d7cc3ad7433f7292287545"} {"question" "q-94807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$1\\cdot A\\ne A$ for all $A\\in K$"] ["text" "addition and scalar multiplication of matrices do not satisfy the distributive laws"] ["text" "addition of matrices is not associative"] ["text" "addition of matrices is not commutative"] ["text" "the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $Y$ be the set of all ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$  such that $x+y\\le 3.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because **multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed.** *  \n\nFor example, $(1,1)\\in Y$ because $1+1=2\\le 3.$ However, if we add the components of $2\\cdot (1,1)=(2,2),$ we get $2+2=4>3.$ So, $2\\cdot (1,1)\\notin Y.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- The zero element in $Y$ is $(0,0).$ $✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is commutative. $\\,✓$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94808" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4648cd819d2f86e7a3e563df5e7fd1d268be7bb1f3d7cc3ad7433f7292287545"} {"question" "q-94808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$Y$ does not contain the zero element"] ["text" "addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$  do not satisfy the distributive laws"] ["text" "addition in $Y$ is not associative"] ["text" "addition in $Y$ is not commutative"] ["text" "multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94808" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $w$ is a vector such that $x+w=0$, then $w=-x$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }A1\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }A4\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4648cd819d2f86e7a3e563df5e7fd1d268be7bb1f3d7cc3ad7433f7292287545"} {"question" "q-94937" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94937" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{A1},\\text{A3}"] ["math" "\\text{A1},\\text{A4}"] ["math" "\\text{A2},\\text{A3}"] ["math" "\\text{A2},\\text{A4}"] ["math" "\\text{A3},\\text{A4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-94937" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{A1},\\text{A4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-106930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $L$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)=ax+1,$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$L$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-106930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$L$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =2$ and $f(x)=x+1,$ then $\\alpha f(x)=2x+2.$ So, $\\alpha f(x)\\notin L$ because the constant term is not $1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in L.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of real valued functions satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-106930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4648cd819d2f86e7a3e563df5e7fd1d268be7bb1f3d7cc3ad7433f7292287545"} {"question" "q-106930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-106930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in L$"] ["text" "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $L$ do not satisfy the distributive laws"] ["text" "addition of functions in $L$ is not associative"] ["text" "addition of functions in $L$ is not commutative"] ["text" "multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-106930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-106940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*If $y$ and $z$ are vectors such that $x+y=z+x$ for some $x\\in V$, then $y=z.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =z+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =z+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =z+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =z &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-106940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =z+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =z+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =z+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =z &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-106940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4648cd819d2f86e7a3e563df5e7fd1d268be7bb1f3d7cc3ad7433f7292287545"} {"question" "q-106940" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068661/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d82a7f07148baf1272145ebd3c2e0227ea0f4f8d14e469c9112d4e209b9d479"} {"question" "q-106940" 